      "segments": [
        {
          "scene": "s01",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 6.5,
          "text": "Can you build a real Iron Man suit? Yes. But not the way the movie does it."
        },
        {
          "scene": "s02",
          "start": 6.5,
          "end": 13.0,
          "text": "No arc reactor. It would cook you alive. So the real suit runs on jet fuel."
        },
        {
          "scene": "s03",
          "start": 13.0,
          "end": 20.0,
          "text": "Six small jet turbines push out about two and a half thousand newtons. Enough to lift a person."
        },
        {
          "scene": "s04",
          "start": 20.0,
          "end": 29.0,
          "text": "But hovering burns fuel fast, so the suit has wings. They swing back for speed, open wide to turn, and tilt up to brake."
        },
        {
          "scene": "s05",
          "start": 29.0,
          "end": 37.0,
          "text": "On paper, that's about twenty minutes from a standing start, and over an hour from a glider-style launch."
        },
        {
          "scene": "s06",
          "start": 37.0,
          "end": 46.0,
          "text": "The legs get a robot exoskeleton so you can stand up in it. I've already designed the knee, and the code is open source."
        },
        {
          "scene": "s07",
          "start": 46.0,
          "end": 52.5,
          "text": "It's dangerous, so nothing goes on me until it's tested, step by step. Follow to watch it happen."
        }
      ]
    },
